ok 10 - fixture: the probe role does not bypass RLS
ok 11 - fixture: all nine tenant tables and the registry hold rows (the world builds a review, an assignment, a decision, a dependency, a snapshot, a schedule, a publication, a token and an accessibility audit summary)
ok 12 - every tenant-scoped Slice 11 table carries a RESTRICTIVE policy for ALL commands that reads and re-checks the verified session party in USING and WITH CHECK [P2-S11-AC-119]
ok 13 - the exclusive writers are bound by RESTRICTIVE INSERT policies (submitter, decider, creator, minter, grantor) and the assignment revoke by a RESTRICTIVE UPDATE policy [P2-S11-AC-119]
ok 14 - the release-seeded preflight registry is written only under the system scope: RESTRICTIVE INSERT, UPDATE and DELETE policies [P2-S11-AC-119]
ok 15 - the CMS RPC-context gate is still present on all ten tables: the session policies are in addition to it, never instead [P2-S11-AC-119]
ok 16 - the four session-scope helpers exist as STABLE SECURITY DEFINER functions of the CMS definer with an empty search_path and no EXECUTE for anyone else [P2-S11-AC-119]
ok 17 - exactly one overload of each session-scope helper exists [P2-S11-AC-119]
ok 18 - row-level security stays enabled and forced on all ten tables [P2-S11-AC-119]
ok 19 - READ allowed: the receipt-derived owner acting in its party reads every row of the nine tenant tables and the registry [P2-S11-AC-007]
ok 20 - READ allowed: the submitter (cms.editor) reads the party's rows [P2-S11-AC-013]
ok 21 - READ allowed: an assigned reviewer reads the party's rows (the five review scopes are the RPC layer's: the recount a decision runs must see every assignment and decision) [P2-S11-AC-013]
ok 22 - READ allowed: the publisher reads the party's rows [P2-S11-AC-019]
ok 23 - READ allowed at the row level: a confirmed member with no CMS capability reads the party's rows (its 403 is the definer RPCs' capability check, proved in their suites) [P2-S11-AC-025]
ok 24 - READ denied: a caller who is not a member of the acting party reads no row of any tenant table (the code-owned registry stays readable) [P2-S11-AC-007]
ok 25 - READ denied: the owner acting in ANOTHER party (its own person party) reads no row of the organization [P2-S11-AC-031]
ok 26 - READ denied: a member whose membership tenure ended reads no row (the predicate re-resolves the membership on every statement) [P2-S11-AC-013]
ok 27 - READ allowed again: once the tenure is confirmed again the same session reads the party's rows (the verdict is per statement, not remembered) [P2-S11-AC-013]
ok 28 - READ denied: a session published for only one of actor and party, or with a malformed party, is not "no session": it reads nothing [P2-S11-AC-031]
ok 29 - READ allowed: a transaction with NO published session (the service paths: sweep, recheck, verifier, takedown) is admitted by the RPC-context gate alone, as before [P2-S11-AC-019]
ok 30 - READ denied: the owner's own session sees nothing outside a CMS RPC context - the gate still applies in addition to the session policy [P2-S11-AC-025]
ok 31 - WRITE allowed: the owner's session updates every row of its party in all nine tenant tables [P2-S11-AC-007]
ok 32 - WRITE denied: a non-member acting in the party updates no row of any tenant table [P2-S11-AC-007]
ok 33 - WRITE denied: the owner acting in another party updates no row of the organization [P2-S11-AC-031]
ok 34 - WRITE denied: a non-member deletes no row of any tenant table [P2-S11-AC-007]
ok 35 - WRITE allowed: with no published session (a service path) the gate alone admits the update, as before [P2-S11-AC-019]
ok 36 - INSERT denied: the owner's session cannot write a row owned by another party into any tenant table (WITH CHECK) [P2-S11-AC-031]
ok 37 - INSERT allowed: a row of the session's own party passes row-level security where no exclusive writer is bound (dependencies, snapshots, publication versions) [P2-S11-AC-019]
ok 38 - INSERT denied: a review is written for the session person only - the submitter cannot attribute a submission to someone else [P2-S11-AC-013]
ok 39 - INSERT allowed: the same review naming the session person passes row-level security [P2-S11-AC-013]
ok 40 - INSERT denied: a decision is written for the session person only - a reviewer cannot record a decision as another reviewer [P2-S11-AC-013]
ok 41 - INSERT allowed: the same decision naming the session reviewer passes row-level security [P2-S11-AC-013]
ok 42 - INSERT denied: a schedule is created for the session person only [P2-S11-AC-019]
ok 43 - INSERT allowed: the same schedule naming the session publisher passes row-level security [P2-S11-AC-019]
ok 44 - INSERT denied: a preview token is minted for the session person only [P2-S11-AC-025]
ok 45 - INSERT allowed: the same token naming the session person passes row-level security [P2-S11-AC-025]
ok 46 - INSERT denied: a member who is not the receipt-derived owner cannot write a reviewer assignment, even naming itself the grantor (CMS-03B-18 is owner-only) [P2-S11-AC-013]
ok 47 - INSERT denied: the owner cannot attribute an assignment to another grantor [P2-S11-AC-013]
ok 48 - INSERT allowed: the owner naming itself the grantor passes row-level security [P2-S11-AC-013]
ok 49 - UPDATE denied: a member who is not the owner revokes (updates) no reviewer assignment [P2-S11-AC-013]
ok 50 - UPDATE allowed: the owner updates (revokes) the party's reviewer assignments [P2-S11-AC-013]
ok 51 - REGISTRY INSERT denied: no human session may write the release-seeded preflight registry [P2-S11-AC-119]
ok 52 - REGISTRY INSERT denied: a transaction with no session and no service-role JWT is not the system scope [P2-S11-AC-119]
ok 53 - REGISTRY INSERT allowed under the system scope (no human session, verified service-role JWT) [P2-S11-AC-119]
ok 54 - REGISTRY UPDATE and DELETE touch no row for a human session [P2-S11-AC-119]
ok 55 - REGISTRY UPDATE reaches every row under the system scope [P2-S11-AC-119]
ok 56 - composition: the real CMS-03B-07 command still schedules an approved review as the publisher under the session policies, attributing the schedule to the publisher [P2-S11-AC-019]
ok 57 - composition: the same command by a non-member is still the concealed NOT_FOUND under the session policies [P2-S11-AC-019]
ok
