ok 10 - cms_verify_preview_token is a private SECURITY DEFINER of the CMS definer (empty search_path) that no API role, service_role included, can execute [P2-S11-AC-075]
ok 11 - the platform_api wrapper is a SECURITY DEFINER of the CMS definer, executable by service_role only, not by PUBLIC, anon or authenticated [P2-S11-AC-075]
ok 12 - both functions are STABLE, so the database itself refuses any insert, update, delete, audit or outbox write [P2-S11-AC-076]
ok 13 - a live token presented by its bound actor verifies [P2-S11-AC-074]
ok 14 - the valid result is exactly PreviewVerificationResult (7 members) [P2-S11-AC-073]
ok 15 - the valid result carries the canonical person as userId, the entry and revision ids, the STORED VersionSet and the exact expiry [P2-S11-AC-073]
ok 16 - the valid result echoes no token hash, plaintext, account id, acting party, context version or route [P2-S11-AC-075]
ok 17 - the verifier writes nothing: token rows (with their xmin), audit, outbox and idempotency are unchanged by valid and denied calls [P2-S11-AC-076]
ok 18 - a repeated verification answers the same document (retry is harmless) [P2-S11-AC-076]
ok 19 - the verifier needs no session or acting context: it answers from the request alone [P2-S11-AC-073]
ok 20 - an unknown token hash is the canonical denial (valid false, five null members, revoked false) [P2-S11-AC-075]
ok 21 - an expired token (15 minutes 10 seconds old) is the canonical denial [P2-S11-AC-074]
ok 22 - a token with ten seconds of life left still verifies (the expiry is exact, not rounded) [P2-S11-AC-074]
ok 23 - a forwarded token presented by another person is the canonical denial, revoked false [P2-S11-AC-075]
ok 24 - another acting-context version is the canonical denial [P2-S11-AC-074]
ok 25 - another route (case, trailing slash, prefix) is the canonical denial: the route must equal the minted one exactly [P2-S11-AC-074]
ok 26 - another locale (case variant or other language) is the canonical denial [P2-S11-AC-074]
ok 27 - another audience is the canonical denial [P2-S11-AC-074]
ok 28 - a token whose minting person lost the entry assignment stops verifying although its row is still active: canonical denial, revoked false [P2-S11-AC-074]
ok 29 - a lapsed standing cms.author grant ends the minting scope: canonical denial (the acting-context version moved as well) [P2-S11-AC-074]
ok 30 - a token of an entry that left `active` is the canonical denial even before its row is revoked [P2-S11-AC-074]
ok 31 - an active reviewer assignee of a review of the revision and an owner-party publisher keep a valid preview [P2-S11-AC-074]
ok 32 - a member with no preview scope on the entry cannot verify a row bound to them (scope is rechecked on every open) [P2-S11-AC-074]
ok 33 - revoking the reviewer assignment ends that reviewer's preview scope [P2-S11-AC-074]
ok 34 - the bound actor presenting a revoked token gets valid false and revoked true, every other member null [P2-S11-AC-075]
ok 35 - another person presenting the same revoked token gets the unknown-token bytes (revoked false): no existence oracle [P2-S11-AC-075]
ok 36 - revoked is true whenever the row exists, is bound to the supplied person and is revoked, whatever else of the binding differs [P2-S11-AC-075]
ok 37 - a revoked token that has also expired still reports revoked for its bound actor [P2-S11-AC-075]
ok 38 - unknown, forwarded, other-actor-revoked and expired denials are the same bytes [P2-S11-AC-075]
ok 39 - every malformed request (missing or extra member, upper-case or short hash, bad uuid, over-long or non-string route, bad locale or audience, null, array, string) is the canonical denial and never an error [P2-S11-AC-077]
ok 40 - a 2,048-character route verifies when presented exactly [P2-S11-AC-074]
ok 41 - route equality is on the exact code points: the NFC route verifies, its NFD spelling is the canonical denial [P2-S11-AC-074]
ok 42 - the stored capability snapshot equals cms_acting_context_version of the minting person (BE04c actingContextVersion), and a minting person with no scope is denied [P2-S11-AC-118]
ok 43 - a granted capability changes the context version: the token verifies only against the version it was minted under (and scope now holds as a publisher) [P2-S11-AC-118]
ok
