ok 11 - control: the review invalidation (superseded revision, archived entry) left the claimed schedules executing; the drifted dependency is found by the executor
ok 12 - an executing schedule whose review was invalidated (a superseded revision, an unavailable entry) is blocked approval_invalidated, never cancelled by the executor (DEC-158(d)) [P2-S11-AC-083]
ok 13 - a frozen manifest that is no longer current invalidates the review (dependency_changed) and blocks the schedule approval_invalidated [P2-S11-AC-083]
ok 14 - a blocked outcome appends no lineage row and emits no publication event: the prior publication stays intact [P2-S11-AC-083]
ok 15 - a review whose version is not the schedule's expected_version blocks the schedule approval_invalidated [P2-S11-AC-080]
ok 16 - a review whose dependency hash differs from the schedule's blocks the schedule approval_invalidated [P2-S11-AC-080]
ok 17 - a review whose activation evidence hash differs from the schedule's blocks the schedule approval_invalidated [P2-S11-AC-080]
ok 18 - a review whose frozen hash is no longer the revision's payload hash blocks the schedule approval_invalidated [P2-S11-AC-080]
ok 19 - none of the four mismatches appended a lineage row or an event, and the blocked outcome left the forged reviews approved (the executor blocks the schedule, it does not rewrite the review) [P2-S11-AC-080]
ok 20 - a schedule whose creator no longer holds an unrevoked cms.publisher grant is blocked publisher_authority_ended [P2-S11-AC-081]
ok 21 - the execute-phase revocation rechecks only the creator's grant and the entry: a counted approver's lapsed grant does not stop a scheduled publication, and MFA is not rechecked (DEC-120) [P2-S11-AC-081]
ok 22 - a failed category (a media reference) blocks the schedule preflight_failed and appends nothing [P2-S11-AC-083]
ok 23 - a blocked accessibility run is a failed category (blocking_finding): the schedule is blocked preflight_failed [P2-S11-AC-083]
ok 24 - control: the entry holds one active v1 head with its event, audit record and evidence summary before the scheduled execution
ok 25 - the scheduled publish over an existing head fails the preflight and the schedule is blocked preflight_failed [P2-S11-AC-083]
ok 26 - the blocked execution left the existing active v1 head, the lineage rows, their events, audit records and evidence summaries exactly as they were: no tombstone, no successor row [P2-S11-AC-083]
ok 27 - absent proof and a failed checker run (unavailable accessibility) each make the schedule failed_retryable with attempt_count 1 and no reason, never a pass [P2-S11-AC-083]
ok 28 - the first retry waits 15 s and the lease is released [P2-S11-AC-082]
ok 29 - each retry is audited without an actor and appends nothing [P2-S11-AC-082]
ok 30 - stale proof (over 60 s), proof bound to other rows and proof from another provider version each refuse the execution with the typed conflict preflight_evidence_stale (DEC-158(c)) [P2-S11-AC-083]
ok 31 - a stale or mis-bound proof consumes no retry state: each schedule is still executing at the claim's version and lease with attempt_count 0 and an unchanged row, and no schedule audit record or other effect exists [P2-S11-AC-083]
ok 32 - the second consecutive failure waits 60 s (attempt_count 2) [P2-S11-AC-082]
ok 33 - the third consecutive failure waits 300 s (attempt_count 3) [P2-S11-AC-082]
ok 34 - the fourth consecutive retryable failure blocks the schedule with retries_exhausted [P2-S11-AC-082]
ok 35 - a blocked schedule is never claimed again [P2-S11-AC-082]
ok
