ok 20 - no outbox event commits: cms.publication.changed.v1 is emitted only by an executed publication [P2-S11-AC-017]
ok 21 - the idempotency reservation is completed with the 202 acceptance [P2-S11-AC-020]
ok 22 - a pending publish makes the revision scheduled (E2) while the review stays approved at its version (the schedule never advances it) [P2-S11-AC-038]
ok 23 - scheduling appends no publication lineage row [P2-S11-AC-017]
ok 24 - an exact replay returns the stored resource, marks x-cms-idempotent-replay and adds no schedule, audit record, event or reservation [P2-S11-AC-020]
ok 25 - a lost-response retry with the same key and a freshly evaluated accessibility proof is a replay, not an IDEMPOTENCY_MISMATCH (the proof is server-built, not part of the command identity) [P2-S11-AC-020]
ok 26 - the same key with a changed audience is IDEMPOTENCY_MISMATCH [P2-S11-AC-020]
ok 27 - even a replay needs a fresh step-up proof (E6: evaluated before the reservation) [P2-S11-AC-047]
ok 28 - unpublish, expire and archive are scheduled against an approved review too [P2-S11-AC-017]
ok 29 - three pending tombstone schedules, one per audience; only a pending PUBLISH makes a revision scheduled (E2) [P2-S11-AC-038]
ok 30 - the revision author may schedule an expire: separation of duties (E11) binds only a publish [P2-S11-AC-107]
ok 31 - a second schedule of the same action, local time, timezone and audience under another key is a CONFLICT and changes nothing [P2-S11-AC-020]
ok 32 - another audience, another local time or another action is a different identity (the audience is part of the key) [P2-S11-AC-020]
ok 33 - a proof 590 s old and one 20 s in the future (skew) are accepted [P2-S11-AC-047]
ok
