ok 10 - the keyset reader and the signed wrapper are private SECURITY DEFINERs nobody can execute; the platform_api wrapper is executable by service_role only [P2-S11-AC-064]
ok 11 - a reviewer reads the default (assigned) queue with no scope or limit given [P2-S11-AC-061]
ok 12 - the page is exactly ReviewQueuePage: items, nextCursor, pageVersion [P2-S11-AC-061]
ok 13 - the assigned scope lists exactly the reviews the caller holds an assignment on, newest update first (the tie pair ordered by review id) [P2-S11-AC-063]
ok 14 - an item is exactly ReviewQueueItem (14 members) [P2-S11-AC-061]
ok 15 - items carry the review state, the caller's own decision (none / approve / reject), the content type label, the revision number and locale and the caller's assignment end [P2-S11-AC-061]
ok 16 - consecutive items strictly descend by (updatedAt at millisecond precision, reviewId): the contract's keyset check holds even for two rows of one millisecond [P2-S11-AC-061]
ok 17 - the tie pair (the larger id has the earlier microsecond) is ordered by id, not by microsecond [P2-S11-AC-061]
ok 18 - pageVersion is the page high-water mark in UTC microseconds and a page that fits has no cursor [P2-S11-AC-064]
ok 19 - the submitted scope lists only reviews the caller submitted; the assigned scope of another reviewer lists only theirs: no review outside the scope is ever listed [P2-S11-AC-063]
ok 20 - assignmentEndsAt is the caller's assignment end for the assigned scope and null for the submitted scope [P2-S11-AC-061]
ok 21 - the state filter narrows the scope: open, approved and invalidated select the right rows and a state with none is the empty page [P2-S11-AC-062]
ok 22 - explicit nulls for cursor, limit, scope and state are the defaults [P2-S11-AC-062]
ok 23 - a non-member, a member with no assignment and a member who submitted nothing get the empty page (pageVersion 1), never an error [P2-S11-AC-063]
ok 24 - another acting party lists nothing of this organisation [P2-S11-AC-063]
ok 25 - three pages of two walk the whole scope exactly once and the last page has no cursor [P2-S11-AC-061]
ok 26 - the cursor is at most 512 characters and a signed six-member envelope (query binding, last position, expiry, key id, signature) [P2-S11-AC-064]
ok 27 - a cursor of another caller, scope, state or page size, a tampered signature or payload, a correctly signed forgery with a foreign binding, an expired and an over-lived cursor are all CONFLICT (restart from the first page) [P2-S11-AC-065]
ok 28 - a non-base64, non-string, empty or over-long cursor, an envelope with an unknown member and a correctly signed payload with a malformed position are INVALID_REQUEST (400) [P2-S11-AC-065]
ok 29 - a limit outside 1..50, a string or a fraction is VALIDATION_FAILED at /limit [P2-S11-AC-062]
ok 30 - an unknown scope or state is VALIDATION_FAILED at its pointer and any other query member (also an ownership claim) is INVALID_REQUEST [P2-S11-AC-062]
ok 31 - without an active Vault signing key the queue fails closed with DEPENDENCY_UNAVAILABLE [P2-S11-AC-065]
