ok 10 - cms_get_entry_workflow and its scope and action helpers are private SECURITY DEFINERs of the CMS definer nobody can execute; the platform_api wrapper is executable by service_role only [P2-S11-AC-052]
ok 11 - an entry assignee reads the workflow of a draft entry [P2-S11-AC-049]
ok 12 - the document is exactly EntryWorkflowResource (7 members) [P2-S11-AC-049]
ok 13 - the entry meta carries the aggregate version (the If-Match operand) and the revision its derived state, true content hash, locale, schema version and current-draft flag [P2-S11-AC-049]
ok 14 - the preparation serves the manifest, its hash, the version set, the risk class and the workflow policy exactly as the server rebuilds them, so a form can echo them unmodified [P2-S11-AC-089]
ok 15 - the submit-phase preflight lists all seventeen categories in registry order and passes with healthy evidence [P2-S11-AC-096]
ok 16 - a draft with no review, schedule or publication offers the assignee submit_review and preview [P2-S11-AC-049]
ok 17 - the document carries no author, assignee, owner, party or account identifier [P2-S11-AC-051]
ok 18 - absent, stale, other-provider and mis-bound evidence degrade the accessibility result to unavailable / checker_failed inside the report and never fail the read [P2-S11-AC-053]
ok 19 - blocked evidence is a failed blocking_finding and the rest of the preparation is identical whatever the proof [P2-S11-AC-096]
ok 20 - an owner-party publisher reads the draft but gets no preparation (only an assignee may submit) and may preview [P2-S11-AC-051]
ok 21 - an entry editor assignee gets the preparation too [P2-S11-AC-051]
ok 22 - a reviewer assignee reads the entry: the revision is derived `submitted`, the latest review is served with its frozen candidate, and they may record a decision and preview [P2-S11-AC-051]
ok 23 - the owner of the entry (an assignee) sees assign_reviewer and preview, and no preparation for a revision under review [P2-S11-AC-054]
ok 24 - an approved revision offers its owner-party publisher schedule, preview and publish [P2-S11-AC-054]
ok 25 - a pending publish schedule makes the revision `scheduled` (E2): the schedule is listed, schedule is no longer offered but publish still is [P2-S11-AC-054]
ok 26 - at most 16 schedules (newest first, a blocked one with its reason code) and 64 publications are served; a published revision is derived `published` [P2-S11-AC-050]
ok 27 - a publication row carries its lineage id, own id, sequence, derived state (superseded / active / revoked), action, hash and projectionState pending (never converged) [P2-S11-AC-050]
ok 28 - no revisionId serves the current draft; an older revision is served with isCurrentDraft false and no preparation [P2-S11-AC-050]
ok 29 - a confirmed member with no workflow read scope (an unassigned reviewer, a member with no capability) is 403 capability_missing [P2-S11-AC-051]
ok 30 - a non-member, an absent entry, a revision of another entry, an absent revision, an archived entry and another acting party are one indistinguishable NOT_FOUND [P2-S11-AC-051]
ok 31 - a held entry is readable, offers no action and reports the revocation category as entry_unavailable [P2-S11-AC-051]
ok 32 - an unknown member, a missing or malformed id and a non-object proof are INVALID_REQUEST [P2-S11-AC-050]
ok 33 - the read writes nothing: reviews, assignments, decisions, reservations, audit, events, tokens, schedules, publications and entry versions are unchanged by every read above [P2-S11-AC-053]
ok
