ok 7 - cms_assign_editorial_reviewer is a private SECURITY DEFINER of the CMS definer (empty search_path) that no API role, service_role included, can execute [P2-S11-AC-070]
ok 8 - the platform_api wrapper is a SECURITY DEFINER of the CMS definer, executable by service_role only, not by PUBLIC, anon or authenticated [P2-S11-AC-070]
ok 9 - the shared review-authority helpers are private definers with no API-role execute [P2-S11-AC-069]
ok 10 - the stored assignment reason is bounded in Unicode code points, not octets (DEC-158(b)) [P2-S11-AC-068]
ok 11 - the receipt-derived owner creates a reviewer assignment on an open review [P2-S11-AC-067]
ok 12 - the resource is exactly EditorialReviewAssignmentResource: meta, reviewId, state, capability, actions, window, reason [P2-S11-AC-067]
ok 13 - a created assignment is active at version 1, confers exactly read and decide on this review and carries a null reason when none was given [P2-S11-AC-067]
ok 14 - the window ends at the requested expiry, after it starts and within seven days [P2-S11-AC-068]
ok 15 - the response names no reviewer, grantor, owner, party or account identifier [P2-S11-AC-069]
ok 16 - the row stores the server-resolved reviewer and grantor, the fixed capability and actions, and the requested window [P2-S11-AC-119]
ok 17 - creating an assignment leaves the review version, state and decision count unchanged [P2-S11-AC-070]
ok 18 - exactly one audit record is committed for the creation [P2-S11-AC-070]
ok 19 - exactly one identifier-only cms.entry.review-changed.v1 is committed, aggregated on the review at its unchanged version [P2-S11-AC-070]
ok 20 - the idempotency reservation is completed with the command [P2-S11-AC-070]
ok 21 - an exact replay returns the stored response unchanged [P2-S11-AC-071]
ok 22 - the replay adds no assignment, audit record, outbox event or reservation [P2-S11-AC-071]
ok 23 - the same key with a changed request is IDEMPOTENCY_MISMATCH [P2-S11-AC-071]
ok 24 - revoking returns the same assignment, revoked, at version 2 [P2-S11-AC-067]
ok 25 - the revoke moves only the assignment (active -> revoked, version + 1); the review is untouched [P2-S11-AC-070]
ok 26 - exactly one audit record is committed for the revoke [P2-S11-AC-070]
ok 27 - the create and the revoke each emitted one review-changed event, both at the unchanged review version [P2-S11-AC-070]
ok 28 - revoking an already revoked assignment is a 409 conflict [P2-S11-AC-068]
ok 29 - revoking a missing assignment is 404 [P2-S11-AC-068]
ok 30 - an assignment of another review is indistinguishable from a missing one [P2-S11-AC-068]
ok 31 - the refused foreign revoke changed nothing [P2-S11-AC-071]
ok 32 - after a revoke the same reviewer can be assigned again (only an active row occupies the unique slot) [P2-S11-AC-119]
ok 33 - a 256-code-point reason (512 octets) is accepted and stored verbatim [P2-S11-AC-068]
ok 34 - a reason of 257 code points, an empty reason, a non-NFC reason and a non-string reason are each VALIDATION_FAILED at /reason (refused, never normalized) [P2-S11-AC-068]
ok 35 - no SafeText exclusion applies to an assignment reason: markup characters and a newline are accepted (DEC-158(b)) [P2-S11-AC-068]
ok 36 - a stale (> 600 s), future (> 30 s), unverified, absent or malformed proof is STEP_UP_REQUIRED, and it is evaluated before concealment (a hidden review is not disclosed) [P2-S11-AC-071]
ok 37 - the step-up refusals reserved no idempotency record and changed no state [P2-S11-AC-071]
ok 38 - a proof 590 s old and a proof 20 s in the future (within the 600 s window and the 30 s skew) are accepted [P2-S11-AC-071]
ok
