ok 11 - cms_record_review_decision is a private SECURITY DEFINER of the CMS definer (empty search_path) that no API role, service_role included, can execute [P2-S11-AC-016]
ok 12 - the platform_api wrapper is a SECURITY DEFINER of the CMS definer, executable by service_role only, not by PUBLIC, anon or authenticated [P2-S11-AC-016]
ok 13 - the assigned reviewer approves an open review [P2-S11-AC-011]
ok 14 - the response is exactly EditorialReviewResource (17 members) [P2-S11-AC-011]
ok 15 - the single required approve reaches approved at version 2 with decidedAt set and the frozen policy evidence [P2-S11-AC-109]
ok 16 - the response carries no reviewer, submitter, author, party or account identifier and no reason text [P2-S11-AC-013]
ok 17 - the decision row stores the server-derived reviewer, slot, assignment, MFA instant, frozen reviewed hash, reason and its SHA-256 comment hash [P2-S11-AC-109]
ok 18 - exactly one audit record and one identifier-only cms.entry.review-changed.v1 at the new review version commit with the decision [P2-S11-AC-016]
ok 19 - the idempotency reservation is completed with the decision [P2-S11-AC-014]
ok 20 - an exact replay returns the stored response and adds no decision, audit record, event or reservation [P2-S11-AC-014]
ok 21 - the same key with a changed reason is IDEMPOTENCY_MISMATCH [P2-S11-AC-014]
ok 22 - a second attempt on the approved review is review_not_open [P2-S11-AC-108]
ok 23 - a reject sets the review rejected immediately and terminally at version 2 [P2-S11-AC-109]
ok 24 - the reject row carries the base slot capability cms.reviewer [P2-S11-AC-121]
ok 25 - a rejected review accepts no further decision [P2-S11-AC-108]
ok 26 - the first of two approvals leaves the review open at version 2 with no decidedAt [P2-S11-AC-109]
ok 27 - one human records at most one decision per review [P2-S11-AC-108]
ok 28 - the second distinct approver reaches the required count: approved at version 3 with two distinct qualifying approvers [P2-S11-AC-109]
ok 29 - the first rejection ends a review that already holds an approval; the approve still recounts but cannot approve it [P2-S11-AC-109]
ok 30 - a base-only reviewer approves first: the base slot, the review stays open (one approval still possible for the specialist slot) [P2-S11-AC-109]
ok 31 - a second base-only approve is refused specialist_slot_unsatisfiable (no approval left for the unfilled specialist slot) and changes nothing [P2-S11-AC-109]
ok 32 - the specialist approves: the first unfilled specialist slot they hold is satisfied and the review is approved [P2-S11-AC-109]
ok 33 - when the specialist slot is already filled by a counted approver a second specialist fills the base slot [P2-S11-AC-109]
ok 34 - a reject is never refused on the specialist-slot ground [P2-S11-AC-109]
ok
