ok 12 - the table carries exactly the write guard and the append-only guard [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 13 - the columns are the envelope, the command reference (the exact audit event, the optional outbox event) and exactly the five summary members (no finding text, no binding hash) [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 14 - the audit event id is NOT NULL, UNIQUE and a foreign key to audit_private.audit_events; the outbox event id is a separate nullable column [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 15 - the outcome is the BE05c run state (healthy, blocked, failed) and the operation is one of the four evidence-carrying commands [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 16 - the recorder and the two audit-writing helpers are private SECURITY DEFINERs of the CMS definer with no API-role execute [P2-S11-AC-101]
true
ok 17 - cms_record_audit_event answers the exact id of the audit row it wrote; cms_emit_event_ids answers the exact audit and outbox ids of the pair it wrote [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 18 - control: the submission with healthy evidence commits
ok 19 - exactly one summary row is written for the submission [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 20 - the row stores the command, the review, the revision, the owner and exactly {checkerKey, checkerVersion, outcome, blockingCount, inputHash} [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 21 - the row references the command's outbox event in its own optional column [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 22 - the row is keyed to the exact audit event of the command (audit_event_id), not by a shared correlation id [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 23 - the review response does not echo the evidence hashes [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 24 - an exact replay writes no second summary row [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 25 - control: blocked evidence fails the preflight, a failed run and absent evidence are unavailable [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 26 - the refused commands (blocked, failed run, no evidence) wrote no summary row [P2-S11-AC-101]
true
ok 27 - a summary row is never updated [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 28 - a summary row is never deleted [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 29 - a write outside the CMS RPC context is refused before any constraint [P2-S11-AC-101]
true
